		sign: "Aries",
		month: "2026-10",
		overview: "Venus enters Libra on the 25th. This is your seventh house, where a contract is only as good as the mood in the room when it was signed. Notice the ground first, because the person across the table hears the offer differently than it was meant, and only then what the sense of what is worth having wants from it.",
		love: "Because Venus turns retrograde on the 3rd, your eighth house is the part that moves. Since joint holdings get settled, and what has run out gets ended properly, the sense of what is worth having gets tested rather than admired. There is more, and it is that Pluto turns direct on the 16th, arriving in the eleventh house you keep friendships and future goals in. The grip that will not loosen counts for less than it thinks here, because other people carry the parts of a plan nobody owns alone. Going without the request put to the people who can actually answer it costs more in your eleventh house than it saves anywhere else. A second thread runs through this, and Venus enters Libra on the 25th, settling into your seventh house, where two names sit on one lease, one invoice or one promise, with the pull toward what is pleasant beneath all of it. The preference nobody argues with reads differently in a place where the argument that never gets finished is the one the marriage rests upon. Your eighth house wants one thing above the rest, and it wants one ending finished properly instead of left half open.",
		career: "The First Quarter Moon falls in Capricorn on the 18th. Your tenth house is where the title on the card and the work under it are graded separately. Since the public record keeps every promise that was made out loud, the instinct gets tested rather than admired. Partway through that, Mercury turns retrograde on the 24th, bringing the question being asked into your eighth house, where what was shared has to be untangled before it can be ended. Given that the joint account, the inheritance papers and the tax return get read line by line, the running commentary is the wrong thing to lead with. Going without the plain total of what is owed and owned costs more in your eighth house than it saves anywhere else. Nothing else in your tenth house works without a result finished to the level it will be judged by.",
		health: "Mars trines Neptune on the 2nd, bringing the readiness to start into your first house, where a habit of standing a certain way turns into a reputation without anyone deciding it should. The part that refuses to wait does not survive contact with the pull toward what is not literal unchanged. Notice the ground first, because the entrance is the argument, and everything after it is footnotes, and only then what the drive wants from it. The other half of it is that the New Moon falls in Libra on the 10th, testing the first reaction against your seventh house, where what one partner leaves unsaid, the other one fills in, usually wrongly. Nothing has surfaced yet, which is the correct condition for a beginning and not a sign of delay. Nothing else in your seventh house works without the other side of it described as they would describe it. After that, Mars and Saturn settle into a trine on the 16th, at the level of your first house, the one for identity and self-expression. The useful move is toward the version of this that survives being said out loud.",
		finance: "Venus turns retrograde on the 3rd, grounding the preference nobody argues with in the eighth house you keep transformation and shared resources in, where the joint account, the inheritance papers and the tax return get read line by line. The pull toward what is pleasant is the pressure here, and the ground it presses on is a place where what was shared has to be untangled before it can be ended. In the same stretch, Pluto turns direct on the 16th, and it registers in the eleventh house you keep friendships and future goals in. Given that other people carry the parts of a plan nobody owns alone, the grip that will not loosen is the wrong thing to lead with. Start with one introduction made instead of a list kept privately. Your eighth house carries this one, because Mercury turns retrograde on the 24th. Forward motion is not what this stretch is for, and forcing it spends the running commentary twice.\n\nNot far behind, Venus leaves Scorpio on the 25th, arriving in your eighth house. Your eighth house asks for one ending finished properly instead of left half open.",
		advice: "Venus leaves Scorpio on the 25th, so the effect shows in the eighth house you keep transformation and shared resources in. Nothing else in your eighth house works without the uncomfortable figure named before anyone acts on it.",
		column: "Your eighth house carries the main event here, and Mercury squares Mars on the 2nd. Whatever the working mind starts, the readiness to start answers for. The running commentary is the pressure here, and the ground it presses on is a place where somebody else holds the other half of the money, the secret or the bed. Next to that, Mars draws a trine to Neptune on the 2nd, grounding the drive in the fifth house you keep romance, creativity, and joy in, where the sketchbook, the guitar and the dating app compete for the same hour. Two different jobs are being done here, one by the part that refuses to wait and one by the pull toward what is not literal. Going without an hour spent on something with no useful outcome costs more in your fifth house than it saves anywhere else. While that is still running, Venus turns retrograde on the 3rd, felt through the eighth house you keep transformation and shared resources in. Where what two parties hold together gets divided or deepened, the sense of what is worth having is either the tool or the obstacle.\n\nBecause Mars stands opposite Pluto on the 3rd, your fifth house is the part that moves. The half that is not being owned gets carried by somebody else, and here that half is the pressure underneath. There is more, and it is that the Sun opposes Saturn on the 4th. Your seventh house is where the terms of a shared thing get set, with somebody else in the room. The part that wants to be seen is set against the weight of what is already owed here. The half that is not being owned gets carried by somebody else, and here that half is the standard being applied. Everything here comes down to a commitment narrowed to what both people can actually keep. Partway through that, Mars reaches a sextile with Uranus on the 7th, with your fifth house taking it. Within reach at this angle, one wants the argument closed rather than managed and the other wants the rule broken cleanly rather than bent, and the offer covers both.\n\nThen the New Moon falls in Libra on the 10th, sitting in your seventh house. Given that a contract is only as good as the mood in the room when it was signed, the first reaction is the wrong thing to lead with. In the same stretch, Pluto turns direct on the 16th, settling into your eleventh house, where a favor asked of a friend costs more than the same favor bought, with the grip that will not loosen beneath all of it. The thing nobody names counts for less than it thinks here, because a wider circle decides what is possible, and the plan runs past the immediate. Nothing else in your eleventh house works without the shared goal stated plainly enough to be joined. Not far behind, Mars and Saturn settle into a trine on the 16th, so the effect shows in the same house.\n\nA second thread runs through this, and Mercury turns retrograde on the 24th, arriving in your eighth house. Notice the ground first, because a debt outlives the reason anyone took it, and only then what the question being asked wants from it. Your eighth house carries this one, because Venus leaves Scorpio on the 25th. The preference nobody argues with reads differently in a place where what was shared has to be untangled before it can be ended. Settle on the uncomfortable figure named before anyone acts on it.",
