						long: "The Sesquiquadrate (135 degrees, also called the sesqui-square or trioctile) combines the energies of the square and the semi-square. While the semi-square creates internal irritation, the sesquiquadrate tends to project tension outward, manifesting as conflicts with external circumstances or other people. It produces a sense of being stuck or thwarted, where the desired outcome remains just out of reach. This aspect often correlates with situations requiring compromise or redirection rather than direct confrontation. When handled maturely, it teaches adaptability and the wisdom of knowing when to push forward and when to find an alternate route.",
